SCIENCE/P-F APPROVE — exact 21,328-byte artifact, SHA-256 bdd7e29edb509a08eb0c125a7b9e8d07ab10f23985234119a38c952b49ed54bc.

Focused re-review confirms both priced blocks are repaired:
- contiguous cells/boundaries, semantic artifacts with overlapping/discontinuous supports, and many-to-many incidence/compatibility are separate identity-bound layers in family, fixed view, report, and DoD;
- baseline construction and fixed-view qualification are source-blind, exclude source/alignment outputs from proposal/pruning/ranking/qualification, bind a feature-use lineage ledger, and keep any source-informed child visibly non-primary;
- route, conformance, authenticity, use admission, calibration, and optional provider identity remain separate;
- the dependency points to the adopted construction-integrity artifact by bead, not a returned revision number.

P/F remains correct: present zeroes and sparse membership survive, visible branches are not renormalized, remainder is retained, external states stay distinct, Viterbi is only a summary, and omission is not inferred from low source mass.

The playback correction also preserves the scientific packet: the shareable static artifact carries verified PTS and a path-free command template, while a separate local runtime receives and re-verifies the movie path without recording it.

No remaining blocker in my assigned review seat.
